3. [The claim I want attacked / nodes/_otr_video_engines/ghost_signal_prompt.py:128-140] Diagnosis of the v2 regression vs alternative mechanisms.
   Defect: The diagnosis that "legibility tracks concrete nouns" is accurate in identifying why SD1.5 failed (v2 mode laws literally requested "an abstract signal field filling the composition", painting texture). However, the regression was amplified by two coupled mechanisms:
   (a) Prompt compression: Prompts shrank from 208-317 chars down to 164-203 chars (32-43 CLIP tokens). In CLIP ViT-L/14, shorter active token sequences concentrate softmax attention; when the few active tokens are abstract ("waveform", "emblem"), texture generation dominates.
   (b) Negative prompt imbalance: The negative prompt (`compose_ghost_negative`, lines 616-646) heavily penalizes human deformities ("bad anatomy, deformed, extra limbs"). With CFG 8.0, when the positive prompt lacked a concrete figurative subject, negative guidance pushed the sampler away from figurative structures into pure geometric abstraction.
   Fix: No code change required; maintain v2.1's concrete framing laws (`GHOST_MODE_LAWS_V2`) and prop motifs, ensuring front-anchored concrete nouns balance the active negative channels.

